  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:</i>&nbsp;<i><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>Designed as a long-barreled Slugthrower Rifle, the Czerka Adventurer is used by bounty hunters because of its high accuracy at long-range. Unlike other <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Slugthrower_Rifles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Slugthrower Rifles\">Slugthrower Rifles</a>, the Adventurer fills its firing chamber with a rich oxidizer as the bullet fires, propelling it faster to give it a longer range and a higher punch. </p><p>Bounty hunters also prize the Adventurer Slugthrower for its ability to easily break down and be stashed inside a small portable container. An Adventurer Slugthrower can be disassembled or reassembled quickly using a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Move_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Move Action\">Move Action</a>. </p><p>Adventurer Slugthrowers don't need <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Packs\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Power Packs\">Power Packs</a>; instead, they employ clips that hold 20 slugs apiece. Clips cost 40 credits, and weigh 0.2 kg. </p><p><b>Accurate:</b> This weapon takes no penalty when firing at targets at Short&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
